Z||000000||FOCOSEVA||07-17-2001||08:29 PM||||Joe's wife Miriamme called me they other day to tell me my 3800SC wiring harness project is nearly complete. She went on to itemize my bill for me, and said that they would ship my harness and other items as soon as payment is received. Needless to say, I mailed them a check this morning. Although I have waited for this harness for a long time, I have no complaints about "The Fiero Shop" in Ontario. I have seen examples of Joe's work on Fieros, and the quality is remarkable. Granted, his turn-around time may not be the fastest, but considering everything he has going on, he does very well, and the results of his efforts are well worth waiting for.<BR>Curry Obenshain<BR>CaptFiero@aol.com||||reg||7
Z||000001||fiero56||07-17-2001||10:35 PM||||I had the experience of riding in Bill's(BENGAL4) series II s/c 3800 Friday. Even with the 4-speed manual(which I think is the perfect match for that kind of power), he was eaily able to rip the tires loose all the way through second gear, with the clutch already mated. Just hit the throttle, and they break loose. Very fast car, he noticed I was getting scared when we hit 3.5Krpm and that engine doubled in power. Plus, the whine of the s/c was excellent.<P>Bill did have to wait for the car, 15 months to be exact, but he's got a great setup.||||reg||1
